Check reader-v1 RPA producer output, including shrink LRI, Coulomb, and GW
preprocessor input (`KPT.info`, `vxc.txt`, and text LCAO wavefunctions),
for a compact two-atom H `1x1x2` solid.

Reader-v1 requires `symmetry=-1` until a full-to-irreducible mapping is
implemented. The established `velocity_matrix.txt` protocol name is retained
for both versions, including its exception to the new 15-character naming
preference.

The serial run compares stable producer references. The two-rank test checks
rank-owned output and compares KS binary assembly with independent text
wavefunctions from the same run, avoiding gauge-dependent historical data.
It also injects root-only and non-root file-open failures to check MPI abort.
